From: YSPEED firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] spi: mt7621: allow SPI_NO_CS with CS1 held asserted

The YS-GPS-12832 vendor display application drives SPI_CS through sysfs, so it
opens spidev with SPI_NO_CS. Its live POLAR register is 0, i.e. the controller
keeps native CS1 asserted for the whole session, and that is the only state the
panel has ever worked in. Deasserting CS1 here would defeat that.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
@@ -163 +163,3 @@
+	if (spi->mode & SPI_NO_CS)
+		mt7621_spi_set_native_cs(spi, true);
 	return mt7621_spi_prepare(spi, speed);
@@ -323 +325 @@
-	host->mode_bits = SPI_LSB_FIRST;
+	host->mode_bits = SPI_LSB_FIRST | SPI_NO_CS;
